{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:2f721b5ad4f7aaff","name":"Draw or Holster a Weapon","source":{"id":"source:reference-2f721b5ad4f7aaff","title":"Draw or Holster a Weapon","revision":24965,"timestamp":"2024-11-10T16:19:55Z","sha256":"bef3b357f9187c2671b7336a4bd60cb87fade5c8a7da2ac28be54e57a982bb6e","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=24965","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Draw%20or%20Holster%20a%20Weapon&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-2f721b5ad4f7aaff","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Core Rulebook"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Core_Rulebook"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Drawing or Holstering a Weapon is a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Move Action"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Move_Action"},". If you are proficient in a weapon's use, Drawing the weapon always includes any action necessary to activate the weapon (thus, a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Lightsaber"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Lightsaber","referenceId":"reference:987a817de9003439"}," can be Drawn and activated as a single ",{"tag":"a","children":["Move Action"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Move_Action"}," if you are proficient with the weapon). If you have the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Quick Draw"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Quick_Draw","referenceId":"reference:ad3a4bd9344ce557"}," Feat, you can Draw or Holster a Weapon as a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Swift Action"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Swift_Action"}," instead of a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Move Action"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Move_Action"},".\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Jedi Counseling"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Web Enhancements"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Web_Enhancements"}," (",{"tag":"a","children":["Jedi Counseling"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Jedi_Counseling"},")"]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Q:"]}," If a Jedi had the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Quick Draw"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Quick_Draw","referenceId":"reference:ad3a4bd9344ce557"}," Feat and wanted to draw their ",{"tag":"a","children":["Lightsaber"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Lightsaber","referenceId":"reference:987a817de9003439"},", would they still have to use another ",{"tag":"a","children":["Swift Action"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Swift_Action"}," to activate the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Lightsaber"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Lightsaber","referenceId":"reference:987a817de9003439"},"?\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["A:"]}," No. The \"Draw a Weapon\" Action normally includes everything necessary to render that weapon immediately usable, including deactivating the safety on a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Blaster Pistol"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Blaster_Pistol","referenceId":"reference:38dcc06542ba096c"}," and activating a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Lightsaber"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Lightsaber","referenceId":"reference:987a817de9003439"}," or ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vibroblade"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vibroblade","referenceId":"reference:4d5963781a5121d7"},". Weapons are designed to be drawn and armed very quickly, so the GM generally shouldn't require a separate ",{"tag":"a","children":["Action"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Action"}," unless there's some unusual difficulty in play (such as when the wielder isn't proficient with the weapon). Similarly, you don't have to spend a separate ",{"tag":"a","children":["Action"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Action"}," to deactivate or disarm a weapon when you holster it.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["However, it is important to note that this applies only to the actual \"Draw or Holster a Weapon\" Action (that is, moving the weapon either to or from a holster, hanger, sling, and so on). It does not apply when picking up or dropping a weapon, nor does it apply when using the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Stealth"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Stealth","referenceId":"reference:526a40a447ddd7aa"}," Skill to use ",{"tag":"a","children":["Sleight of Hand"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Sleight_of_Hand"}," to get the weapon in your hand without attracting attention. In these cases, you're not getting the weapon in your hand as efficiently as you would when drawing or holstering it.\n"]},"\n","\n","\n","\n","\n\n","\n\n","\n"]}}
